// The control for fw_aftermath_sessions: the host's 20 largest flows in the same window,
// deduplicated the same way (client side srcport + dstip + dstport, max() of the
// cumulative byte counters). Any row = the host was visible to the firewall, so a small
// or empty aftermath is a measurement, not a gap; the largest rows are the yardstick for
// "small". devices > 1 confirms the flows are logged by several FortiGates.
// See references/fortigate.md F3.
// Placeholders: {SRCIP} = the host's address; {T0} = the event time, ISO-8601 UTC.
NetworkFortigateTraffic
| where TimeGenerated between ((datetime("{T0}") - 1m) .. (datetime("{T0}") + 60m))
| where srcip == "{SRCIP}"
| summarize sent = max(sentbyte), rcvd = max(rcvdbyte), dur = max(duration),
    first = min(TimeGenerated), devices = dcount(tostring(devname))
    by srcport, dstip, dstport
| extend total = sent + rcvd
| top 20 by total desc
